 "findings": [
  "With sourced, masked count dipoles the count-implied boost is |beta_MO| ~2.6e-3 (alpha 1.0) to 3.0e-3 (alpha 0.5), 2.1-2.5x the CMB-dipole speed, but poorly constrained: per-axis sd 5e-4 (x), ~2e-3 (y), ~8e-4 (z) for Quaia, 1e-3..1.4e-2 for NVSS; chi2 improvement over the null is only 18.4 (Quaia) + 6.4 (NVSS) for 3 dof each (H_0 vs H_loc: Delta_BIC 2.0 in favour of H_loc, i.e. weak). The legacy 'excess' (|beta| 4-6e-3, chi2 improvement ~210) is not reproduced.",
  "Including the systematics-dominated RACS block restores a larger preference (Delta_BIC(H_0)=21.5) and moves beta_MO (RACS-only beta_eq 1.9e-2); that block is not trusted.",
  "SNe and PV remain uninformative at this level (cost of the count best fit dchi2 ~3.4-4.2 and ~6.5 for 3 dof).",
  "Gaia block: the nuisance design marginalises data entries 0-5 (glide AND spin) with flat priors, so Gaia carries no glide information; the response constants pred[:3]=0.92*beta_MO and pred[6:11]=0.18*sigma compare dimensionless quantities with mas/yr data and have no derivation (a proper-motion transfer needs the H0[mas/yr] scale, the E2-basis projection with the Gram diag 4.8/1.6 and a validated sign convention). NOT fixed: no physical transfer was invented. Without Gaia, H_mix gains only 6 chi2 for 8 parameters (Delta_BIC +52.6): the earlier H_mix gain was Gaia saturation.",
  "H_loc is best by BIC in all runs; H_tilt equals the null (beta_RM enters no channel); SNe ~433/490 and PV ~903/1000 remain adequate."
 ],
 "caveats": [
  "Point estimates; no sampling; no matched-null calibration; synthetic randoms for NVSS; mask systematic enters only as a covariance term; response slopes x are declared proxies; alpha is a declared nuisance (grid 0.5-1.0)",
  "Not the CORE-07 production inference; no claim of departure from FLRW or of a detected excess."
 ],
